s7-2-p6 : Block
s7-2-p6 = prose (cons "A concrete **sequentially consistent** event model makes the admissibility predicate explicit. Let \(E\) be a finite set of read/write events, \(\mathsf{po}\) the per-thread program order, and \(\mathsf{rf}\) the reads-from relation. Define \(\mathsf{Allowed}_{SC}(X)\) to be the type of a total order \(<_X\) on \(E\) extending \(\mathsf{po}\) such that every read observes the latest preceding write to its location in \(<_X\) (or its specified initial value). This is a complete example of a memory-model predicate, not the C++ weak-memory predicate. A C++ atomic or data-race theorem uses the actual chosen C++ execution axioms in place of \(\mathsf{Allowed}_{SC}\); the event structure and observation operations remain constructions." nil)
